From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:00:12 +0200
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: enable the syscon restart handler in
 grx500_defconfig

The RCU node now describes the global software reset as a syscon-reboot
child, but the driver that binds it is behind a menuconfig that defaults
off, so a defconfig kernel still has no restart handler at all and still
hangs in machine_hang() when asked to reboot.

CONFIG_POWER_RESET is a plain menuconfig with no default and has to be
stated before anything under it is reachable; CONFIG_POWER_RESET_SYSCON
then selects MFD_SYSCON, which this configuration already has on for
reset-lantiq.c and the RCU regmap the reboot node borrows from its
parent.

Nothing else in drivers/power/reset belongs here. The board has no
programmable power-off path -- pm_power_off stays NULL and "halt" keeps
parking the CPU, which is the correct outcome for hardware whose only
off switch is the mains.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
index c393e0431518..50280ffee7df 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
@@ -90,6 +90,8 @@ CONFIG_SERIAL_LANTIQ=y
 # CONFIG_HW_RANDOM is not set
 CONFIG_PINCTRL=y
 CONFIG_PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM=y
+CONFIG_POWER_RESET=y
+CONFIG_POWER_RESET_SYSCON=y
 # CONFIG_HWMON is not set
 # CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE is not set
 # CONFIG_HID is not set
